0018:     - The wall pixels form one or more 4-connected one-cell-thick segments.
0019:     - Each wall segment separates exactly two 4-connected background regions.
0020:     Rule
0021:     - Keep all wall pixels unchanged.
0022:     - Label the 4-connected background regions and connect two labels when they
0023:       touch opposite sides of the same wall segment.
0024:     - Color the region containing the lower-left corner grey, then flip between
0025:       grey and green across every wall adjacency.
0026:     Key insight
0027:     - The red walls define a bipartite map of regions; the lower-left background
0028:       region fixes which side of the alternating coloring is grey.
